  {
   "id": "b025",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Executive Summary",
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b026",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Unit 42 has observed a persistent cyberespionage campaign we track as CL-STA-1114. This activity cluster overlaps with activity from a Russian threat actor tracked by other vendors as Void Blizzard and LAUNDRY BEAR.",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b027",
   "page": null,
   "text": "The attackers behind this campaign targeted Zimbra webmail in organizations in the following sectors:",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b028",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Governments",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b029",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Defense",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b030",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Transportation",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b031",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Financial organizations across the following regions:",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b032",
   "page": null,
   "text": "NATO member states",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b033",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Ukraine",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b034",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) countries",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b035",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Africa",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b036",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Unique to this campaign, the group leveraged zero-click phishing emails that exploit a vulnerability in the Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS) webmail platform (CVE-2025-66376). The exploit automatically injects a malicious JavaScript payload without requiring recipient interaction. Once executed, the payload exfiltrates sensitive user data, including login credentials, email archives, and search histories. Threat actors continue to actively target unpatched ZCS instances using CVE-2025-66376.",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b037",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Palo Alto Networks customers are better protected from the threats discussed above through the following products:",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b038",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Cortex Advanced Email Security",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b039",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Advanced URL Filtering and Advanced DNS Security",
   "type": "list",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b040",
   "page": null,
   "text": "If you think you might have been compromised or have an urgent matter, contact the Unit 42 Incident Response team.",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "section": "Executive Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "b041",
   "page": null,
   "text": "Related Unit 42 Topics | Cyberespionage, Phishing, Data Exfiltration",
   "type": "table",
   "table": {
    "rows": [
     [
      "Related Unit 42 Topics",
